{title: Praise the Savior, Ye Who Know Him}
{artist: Thomas Kelly}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Opening}
{key: G}
{tempo: 100}
{time: 3/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (The Covenant Hymnal (Chicago, Illinois: Covenant Press, 1973), # 251)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Praise the [G]Savior, [D]ye who know Him!
[D]Who can [G]tell how much we [D]owe Him?
[G]Gladly let us render [C]to Him
[C]All we [G]are__[D7]__ and [G]have.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]Keep us, [G]Lord, O [D]keep us cleaving
[D]To Thy[G]self, and still be[D]lieving,
[G]Till the hour of our re[C]ceiving
[C]Promised [G]joys__[D7]__ with [G]Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[D]Then we [G]shall be [D]where we would be,
[D]Then we [G]shall be what we [D]should be,
[G]Things that are not now, nor [C]could be,
[C]Soon shall [G]be__[D7]__ our [G]own.
{end_of_verse}
